What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/.../power_cycle_seconds
Date:		November 2026
Contact:		Mark Featherston <mark@embeddedts.com>
Description:
		Writing a positive integer immediately powers off the system and
		restarts it after the requested number of seconds. This does not
		perform an orderly Linux shutdown or sync filesystems; userspace
		must do so before writing. The supported maximum is 42949672 seconds
		on TS-7100/TS-7180 and 16777215 seconds on TS-4100/TS-7553-V2.
		Actual off time depends on the controller's low-power clock.
